# Later rules win, so the catch-all comes first and the exceptions follow it.
* text=auto

# The GEDCOM fixture's CRLF line endings are part of what it tests: GEDCOM requires
# CRLF, and one of the two defects the fixture reproduces is a bare LF among them.
# Without -text, a commit or checkout under core.autocrlf=input rewrites every line
# ending and the fixture stops encoding the distinction it exists for.
*.ged -text

# SQLite databases. Marked binary so git neither normalises nor tries to diff them.
*.ftb binary
*.ftb-shm binary
*.ftb-wal binary
